isobmff-rs
Copyright 2026 Chris Dobbyn

isobmff-rs is a new crate, not a port of one repository. It parses the ISO base media file
format (HEIF, HEIC, AVIF) from the published layouts of ISO/IEC 14496-12, ISO/IEC 23008-12, the
AVIF and AV1-ISOBMFF specifications, and ISO/IEC 21496-1. docs/design.md describes the design.

Third-party code and data
-------------------------

1. libavif 1.4.2 (BSD 2-Clause), github.com/AOMediaCodec/libavif at c5240fc.

   Ported rule: Clap::crop in src/props/image.rs follows avifCropRectFromCleanApertureBox in
   src/avif.c (the exact-fraction clean aperture to crop rectangle rule, including its checks:
   positive denominators below 2^31, integer clap width and height, integer and non-negative left
   and top edges, a rectangle inside the image). The gain map payload checks of
   src/derived.rs (non-zero denominators, max not below min, non-zero gamma, no trailing bytes
   for writer version 0) follow src/gainmap.c and the tmap reader in src/read.c.
   libavif also runs as a CI oracle (tests/parity/c/avif_oracle.c); it is not linked into the
   crate.

